A table becomes a view of the same name: the ledger drops the table on
purpose (its rows go), and schema.sql makes the view, which holds no rows
of its own.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 95);
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE VIEW menu AS SELECT id, name FROM dish;

== ledger
DROP TABLE menu;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's step 1
  step 1
    DROP TABLE menu;
roux: migrating test.db, 1 step
  view `menu`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE VIEW menu AS SELECT id, name FROM dish
